 "project": {
  "format": "bspk-studio-project",
  "id": "air-size-study",
  "name": "Air size study",
  "title": "Air size study \u00b7 how small the teeth go",
  "blurb": "Three gear pairs, 3:1 each, at module 0.6, 0.5, 0.4, cut in 1/16\" delrin with a 0.5 mm end mill on the Air, between three 1/8\" black delrin plates (41.6 x 76.9 mm). Each pinion has the fewest teeth that leave 1 mm of wall round its 3 mm rod. Cut it, spin each pair by hand, and the smallest pair that runs clean sets Beta 2's tooth size. Every hole names a fit, so the press-fit test's sizes drop in once.",
  "source": [
   "Claude, 2026-11-23, from Adam's Beta 2 brief: smallest envelope with 3 mm brass rod, 3 x 6 x 2.5 flanged bearings, acrylic and delrin; all testing on the Air."
